gnancy and breast cancer: a population-based study</article-title><source>Virchows Arch</source><year>2003</year><volume>443</volume><fpage>44</fpage><lpage>50</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12756565</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00428-003-0817-z</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dargent</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Mayer</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lansac</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Carret</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Breast cancer and pregnancy. Apropos of 96 cases followed for 3 and 1/2 years at the Centre Leon Berard, Lyons [in French]</article-title><source>J Gynecol Obstet Biol Reprod (Paris)</source><year>1976</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>783</fpage><lpage>803</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1026759</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bianchi</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Zickwolf</surname><given-names>GK</given-names></name><name><surname>Weil</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Sylvester</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>DeMaria</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Male fetal progenitor cells persist in maternal blood for as long as 27 years postpartum</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>1996</year><volume>93</volume><fpage>705</fpage><lpage>708</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8570620</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.93.2.705</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>O'Donoghue</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Chan</surname><given-names>J</given-names></na